Review of the nine commits from 2026-08-23 (multi-tenant SaaS foundation)
through 2026-09-08 (governance round 4). Fixes below are grouped by root cause.

Tenant Prisma facade returned plain promises (src/lib/prisma.ts)

The facade's model delegates returned eagerly-started native Promises. Prisma's
batch `$transaction([...])` rejects anything whose Symbol.toStringTag is not
"PrismaPromise", so all eight batch call sites threw at runtime — and because
the operations had already started, the earlier statements landed with no
rollback. Reproduced against a real Postgres: setCurrentAcademicYear() threw and
left the association with no current academic year at all.

Affected: bulk attendance save, password reset, invitation acceptance,
set/delete academic year, project-plan activation, task-plan linking.

Delegates are now lazy and PrismaPromise-compatible, matching the contract a
real PrismaClient delegate has. Verified end-to-end: batch transactions run,
roll back atomically on failure, un-awaited calls do no work, and the callback
form and Promise.all still behave.

withClient() was also inert — getClientForRequest() never consulted the
AsyncLocalStorage store it wrote to, so a forced client was silently ignored.
Client resolution now reads that store first.

Deactivation did not revoke access (src/lib/auth.ts)

freshRolesFor() returned null both for "subject is gone/deactivated" and for
"could not determine", and the jwt callback ignored null entirely. A deactivated
account kept its roles until the JWT expired, which defeated the 10-second
refresh the code was built around. The three outcomes are now distinct:
revoked ends the session, unknown keeps the token so a DB blip doesn't sign
everyone out. Login now also requires member.isActive, matching the refresh
check — previously they disagreed.

Missing authorization checks

- POST /api/programs/import had no role check at all, so any signed-in member
  could import into, and upsert over, any section's annual program. Now
  requires hasSectionRW on the target section, like POST /api/programs.
- GET /api/meetings and GET /api/grants exposed board minutes, decisions and
  funder amounts/contacts to any signed-in member. Now gated on
  canViewGovernance, matching every sibling governance route.
- GET /api/family-links returned the whole family graph — names, registration
  numbers and children's photos — to any signed-in member. Now matches its own
  POST guard and its only (admin-gated) consumer.
- GET /api/volunteer-hours self-scoped non-approvers, then let ?memberId=
  overwrite that scope, so any member could read another's record.
- POST /api/notes let any signed-in member attach notes to any member's file.

Suspended tenants read the wrong database (src/lib/tenants.ts)

Routing resolved ACTIVE tenants only, but the proxy deliberately lets a
suspended tenant reach /billing to renew. That page fell back to the primary
platform database, so the renewal screen reported someone else's member count.
SUSPENDED is now routable; PENDING_PROVISIONING and PROVISION_FAILED stay
unroutable since they have no database yet. Access control for suspended
tenants remains the proxy's job.

i18n keys rendering raw to users

74 keys reached t() with no dictionary entry, so screens in the newest features
displayed literal strings like "elections.seats". 68 were call sites missing the
gov. namespace prefix the dictionary already used; 6 were genuinely absent and
are added in both AR and FR. AR/FR parity is now exact (2404/2404) with zero
unresolved keys.

Verification: tsc --noEmit clean, eslint 0 errors (50 pre-existing warnings
unchanged), next build succeeds, and the transaction behaviour is covered by an
end-to-end run against a real Postgres instance.

